<!-- ===== MEET THE TEAM ===== -->
<section class="content-section">
  <div class="content-inner">
    <div class="team-grid">
      <div class="team-card">
        <div class="photo">
          <img src="images/lucinda-thompson.jpg" alt="Lucinda Thompson" onerror="this.parentElement.classList.add('broken')">
          <div class="fallback">L</div>
        </div>
        <div class="info">
          <span class="role">Finance Director</span>
          <h3>Lucinda Thompson</h3>
          <p>An engineer by profession and an active player at LWCC for over a year. As Treasurer, Lucinda oversees the club's financial health, ensuring transparency and managing the funds that support our coaching sessions and tournaments. She's committed to maintaining a strong financial foundation for LWCC's continued success and growth.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="team-card">
        <div class="photo">
          <img src="images/zoya.png" alt="Zoya Boozorginia" onerror="this.parentElement.classList.add('broken')">
          <div class="fallback">Z</div>
        </div>
        <div class="info">
          <span class="role">Founder & Managing Director</span>
          <h3>Zoya Boozorginia</h3>
          <p>The founder and Managing Director of LWCC. A project architect by background, Zoya brings creativity, structure, and vision to every initiative she leads.</p>
          <p>Having learned chess as a child, she rediscovered her passion for the game in adulthood, joining Battersea Chess Club in 2021 and immersing herself in competitive play. Inspired by <em>The Queen's Gambit</em>, she became even more captivated by the beauty and challenge of the game, and as the women she gathered around her grew into a group, she realised it was time to create something lasting.</p>
          <p>Her mission is to make chess accessible, inclusive, and inspiring: encouraging women at all levels to build confidence, connect socially, and compete professionally.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="team-card">
        <div class="photo">
          <img src="images/archi.png" alt="Archi" onerror="this.parentElement.classList.add('broken')">
          <div class="fallback">Ar</div>
        </div>
        <div class="info">
          <span class="role">In-House Coach</span>
          <h3>Archi</h3>
          <p>A passionate chess coach with over 15 years of playing experience. Archi specialises in working with children, helping them build strong thinking skills, confidence, and a love for the game.</p>
          <p>Archi has loved seeing more women take up chess, and understands how intimidating a male-dominated space can feel. She's dedicated to helping women feel confident stepping into it, and her coaching sessions with LWCC have already encouraged more women to join the chess community.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="team-card">
        <div class="photo">
          <img src="images/anna.png" alt="Anna" onerror="this.parentElement.classList.add('broken')">
          <div class="fallback">A</div>
        </div>
        <div class="info">
          <span class="role">Website & Communications Director</span>
          <h3>Anna</h3>
          <p>An aspiring AI engineer and a student at King's College London. Anna built this website and helps run the club's online presence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

